            <hcontainer name="amendedAct" eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3">
              <heading>Family Law Act 1975</heading>
              <hcontainer name="item" eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-1">
                <num>10</num>
                <heading>Subsection 4(1)</heading>
                <content>
                  <p>Insert:</p>
                </content>
                <quotedStructure eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-1__qstr-1" startQuote="“" endQuote="”" from="#" to="#">
                  <content>
                    <p><b><i>Family Law Magistrate of Western Australia</i></b> means a person who holds office concurrently:</p>
                  </content>
                  <paragraph eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-1__qstr-1__para-a">
                    <num>a</num>
                    <content>
                      <p>	(a)	as a magistrate under the <i>Magistrates Court Act 2004</i> of Western Australia; and</p>
                    </content>
                  </paragraph>
                  <paragraph eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-1__qstr-1__para-b">
                    <num>b</num>
                    <content>
                      <p>as the Principal Registrar, or as a Registrar, of the Family Court of Western Australia.</p>
                    </content>
                  </paragraph>
                </quotedStructure>
              </hcontainer>
              <hcontainer name="item" eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-2">
                <num>11</num>
                <heading>Subsection 39(7)</heading>
                <content>
                  <p>Repeal the subsection, substitute:</p>
                </content>
                <quotedStructure eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-2__qstr-1" startQuote="“" endQuote="”" from="#" to="#">
                  <subsection eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-2__qstr-1__subsec-7">
                    <num>7</num>
                    <content>
                      <p>The Governor-General may, by Proclamation, fix a day as the day on and after which proceedings in relation to matters arising under this Part may not be instituted in, or transferred to, a court of summary jurisdiction in a specified State or Territory.</p>
                    </content>
                    <content>
                      <p>(7AAA)	Without limiting the generality of subsection (7), a Proclamation under that subsection may be expressed to apply only in relation to one or more of the following:</p>
                    </content>
                    <paragraph eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-2__qstr-1__subsec-7__para-a">
                      <num>a</num>
                      <content>
                        <p>proceedings of specified classes;</p>
                      </content>
                    </paragraph>
                    <paragraph eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-2__qstr-1__subsec-7__para-b">
                      <num>b</num>
                      <content>
                        <p>the institution of proceedings in, or the transfer of proceedings to, a court of summary jurisdiction in a specified part of a State or Territory;</p>
                      </content>
                    </paragraph>
                    <paragraph eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-3__item-2__qstr-1__subsec-7__para-c">
                      <num>c</num>
                      <content>
                        <p>the institution of proceedings in, or the transfer of proceedings to, a court of summary jurisdiction constituted in a specified way.</p>
                      </content>
                    </paragraph>
                  </subsection>
                </quotedStructure>
              </hcontainer>
